---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";

const email = "support@getclicker.me";
---

<Base
  title="Support — Clicker"
  description="Help with Clicker: finding your Roku, fixing buttons that don’t respond, managing or restoring a plan, and how to reach us."
>
  <article class="container prose">
    <p class="ecp">support</p>
    <h1>Support</h1>
    <p>
      Stuck? Most problems are fixed by one of the steps below. If not,
      email <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a> with your iPhone model,
      iOS version, and Roku model, and we’ll get back to you.
    </p>

    <h2>Clicker can’t find my Roku</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Your phone and Roku must be on the same Wi-Fi network.</li>
      <li>
        Guest networks and hotel Wi-Fi often block device-to-device traffic.
        Use your main home network.
      </li>
      <li>A VPN on your phone can block local discovery. Turn it off and rescan.</li>
      <li>
        Clicker needs the Local Network permission. Check it in iOS Settings →
        Clicker → Local Network.
      </li>
      <li>
        Wake the Roku by pressing a button on its physical remote, then rescan.
      </li>
      <li>
        As a last resort, connect by IP address. On the Roku, Settings →
        Network → About shows it.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>It finds my Roku, but buttons don’t work</h2>
    <p>
      Your Roku is probably set to block control from mobile apps. With the
      Roku’s own remote, go to Home → Settings → System → Advanced system
      settings → Control by mobile apps → Network access, and choose
      <strong>Default</strong> (not Limited).
    </p>

    <h2>My Roku stopped responding</h2>
    <p>
      It may have been turned off, or your router gave it a new address. Pull
      down on the Devices screen to rescan. Clicker recognizes your Roku by
      its serial number and reconnects.
    </p>

    <h2>Plans and billing</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Restore a purchase:</strong> in Clicker, open Settings and tap
        Restore Purchases, signed in with the same Apple Account you bought
        with.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Cancel the weekly plan:</strong> open the iOS Settings app,
        tap your name, then Subscriptions → Clicker. Clicker’s own Settings
        screen also has a Manage Subscription button.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Refunds:</strong> payments go through Apple, so refunds do
        too. Request one at{" "}
        <a href="https://reportaproblem.apple.com" rel="noopener">reportaproblem.apple.com</a>.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Email <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a>. We read every message.
    </p>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .prose {
    max-width: 680px;
    padding-block: calc(var(--space) * 10);
  }

  .prose h1 { margin-top: calc(var(--space) * 3); }

  .prose h1 + p { margin-top: calc(var(--space) * 2); }

  .prose h2 {
    font-size: 24px;
    margin-top: calc(var(--space) * 5);
    margin-bottom: calc(var(--space) * 1.5);
  }

  .prose p + p { margin-top: calc(var(--space) * 2); }

  .prose ul {
    padding-left: 1.25em;
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space);
  }
</style>
